		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4807&amp;p=35381#p35381"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I noticed a problem on my TYT MD-UV390. If the radio is in FM mode, squelch is set to open (or set to 0) and has an active aprs option (smart option), it freezes at the time of transmit aprs. The only thing that helps is the radio reboot.</div></blockquote>I just tried, and it works (no freeze, see below).<br><br>If you transmit on the same frequency as the current channel, with an opened squelch, it will try to send the APRS beacon, but fails, as it checks if there is some signal (waiting for 2 secs).<br>And it will do that, again and again.<br>That slows down the responsiveness of the UI, but that doesn't really freeze it at all.<br><br>Finally, I don't see the point of doing this.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Sun Jan 26, 2025 3:34 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
